2026-10-12T16:52:37.4160400Z @@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4160602Z +# status Worker service
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4160813Z +
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4162000Z +Generated from the API template. The Worker owns `cloudflare.config.ts` and uses the shared contracts and observability packages. Storage: Volatile sample — resets when the Worker restarts. No resource provisioning runs during setup or build.
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4163097Z +
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4163296Z +From the workspace root:
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4163519Z +
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4163692Z +```console
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4163884Z +pnpm dev -- status
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4164136Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status test
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4164493Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status test:runtime
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4164842Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status build
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4165215Z +pnpm deploy:preflight -- --target status --environment local
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4165603Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status cf --help
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4165897Z +```
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4166079Z +
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4167393Z +`GET /status` reports `{ "ok": true, "service": "status" }` with `Cache-Control: no-store`; only that exact GET path is a status probe. `GET /health` reports readiness; the generated `/api/notes` sample validates input and creates, lists and deletes notes. Local writes are allowed. Remote artifacts deny unauthenticated writes; a service without D1 uses volatile memory and resets on restart.
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4168755Z +
2026-10-12T16:52:37.4170276Z +For approved dev delivery, configure an existing account/token and explicitly approved domain in the sole config, plus IDs for any selected resources. Run the dev preflight, then the workspace's checked `deploy` entry with its approved health URL. Local preflight/build do not establish remote deployment or connectivity. See [Cloudflare instructions](../../docs/cloudflare.md).
